# Contributing to FreeLaunch

Thank you for your interest in FreeLaunch. This document explains how to propose changes so they are easier to review and accept.

Canonical repository: [gitverse.ru/freelaunch/FreeLaunch](https://gitverse.ru/freelaunch/FreeLaunch)  
GitHub is a read-only mirror of GitVerse.

## How to propose changes

1. **Bugs and feature requests**  
   Prefer the [bugtracker](https://bt.freelaunch.su/).  
   On GitVerse you may also open an issue or start a discussion before coding large changes.

2. **Small fixes**  
   Fork the repository on GitVerse, create a branch from `master`, open a merge request (MR) into `master`.

3. **Larger changes**  
   Please discuss the idea first (bugtracker / discussion / issue), so we can agree on scope and approach before a large MR.

Do not open pull requests against the GitHub mirror for upstream inclusion — they will not be merged there.

## Merge request checklist

Please include in the MR description:

- [ ] What problem this solves (link to bugtracker issue / GitVerse issue if any)
- [ ] How you tested the change (OS version, steps)
- [ ] Notes for the reviewer (risks, follow-ups, intentional omissions)

Keep the MR focused: one topic per MR when practical. Avoid unrelated reformatting.

## Development environment

| Item | Value |
|------|--------|
| IDE | Embarcadero Delphi 12 Athens (Community Edition is fine) |
| Framework | VCL, Win32 |
| Output | `build/bin/FLaunch.exe` (see project settings) |

Notes:

- Community Edition does **not** build from the command line — compile in the IDE.
- Day-to-day work uses the **Debug** configuration. Use **Release** only for packaging a release build, then switch back to Debug.
- Zip packaging: `build/makezip.bat` (requires a previously built executable).

## Code guidelines

- Source and comments are written in **English**.
- Prefer a **minimal diff**: change only what the task needs; do not reformat unrelated code.
- Form modules: `*FormModule.pas` + `.dfm`; shared logic lives in `FL*.pas` modules.
- Match existing naming, structure, and style in nearby code.
- Design-time captions in `.dfm` files are optional placeholders for the IDE designer; runtime UI text comes from language files (`.lng`) via `FLLanguage`.

## Commit messages

- Use short, clear messages in English (imperative or past tense is fine if consistent with nearby history).
- Explain *why* when it is not obvious from the diff.
- Do not mix unrelated fixes in one commit when they can be split cleanly.

## Review and expectations

- Maintainers review MRs as time allows; there is no fixed SLA.
- Feedback may request smaller commits, tests on specific Windows versions, or API/compatibility notes (for example Windows 7).
- CI may mirror accepted `master` changes to GitHub automatically; you do not need to update the mirror yourself.

